Subject: [PATCH] daynight: always-start stats worker; persist + record forced mode; derive boot running_mode from it
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable)

Fixes, on T23 / isp_bypass=true builds, three problems with forced day/night:
 (A) AE/day-night telemetry (total_gain, ev, ae_luma, brightness_percent) read
     -1 for the whole process life when daynight.enabled=false, because the
     DayNightWorker -- the sole writer of those values -- was only started when
     enabled. Fix: always start the worker; automatic switching stays gated on
     daynight.enabled inside the loop.
 (B) A forced mode did not survive reboot, and the live mode was misreported.
     daynight.force_mode was not a persisted config key; the worker never tagged
     the live mode for a forced camera (it reported "unknown"); and the ISP was
     hard-forced to Day at the end of IMPSystem::init(). Fix: register
     daynight.force_mode as a persisted string key; have the worker RECORD it
     (current + live_mode "day"/"night", and suppress auto-inference) without
     applying it on the live pipeline.
 (C) A forced color/mono mode did not take at boot. On this sensor a
     set_running_mode at the END of init does NOT stick, while the one applied
     early in init (right after the hflip/vflip block) does. Fix: derive
     image.running_mode from daynight.force_mode BEFORE that early
     set_running_mode, so a forced mode lands where it actually takes effect; the
     end-of-init call becomes a harmless re-assert (no longer hardcoded Day).

Design -- daynight.force_mode is the SINGLE source of truth. From it:
  * color/mono (ISP running_mode) is derived in IMPSystem::init() (this patch);
  * the live/reported mode is set by the worker (this patch);
  * the IR-CUT filter + IR LED are set by the boot IR-CUT init (S56ircut, a
    companion rootfs change) which reads the same daynight.force_mode.
The worker is RECORD-ONLY at startup: it never calls apply_mode() for a persisted
mode, so there is no apply() on a settling cold-boot encoder (which tore the
stream down) and no boot-time day->night flip. Runtime JSON-API force-mode
requests are unaffected and still apply_mode() immediately.

Verified to apply cleanly to the pinned commit (git apply -p1 and patch -p1).

